@startuml SKVP_State_Machine
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam state {
    BackgroundColor LightBlue
    BorderColor DarkBlue
    ArrowColor Black
}

title Sovereign Kernel Verification Protocol (SKVP) State Machine
caption Strict separation of successful commit tracks vs. null space isolated tracks.

|Orchestrator|
|Verifier|
|Executor|
|Auditor|

|Orchestrator|
[*] --> PROPOSED : New Request

|Verifier|
PROPOSED --> VERIFYING : VERIFY_REQUEST

state VERIFYING {
    state "Fast Path Checks\n(HMAC, Nonce, Parent)" as Fast
    state "SDI & Invariants" as SDI
    state "IVC Proof Check" as IVC

    Fast --> SDI : OK
    SDI --> IVC : OK
}

VERIFYING --> COMMITTABLE : all_checks_pass\n[T < T_full]
VERIFYING --> REFUSED : any_check_fail\n[or timeout]

|Executor|
COMMITTABLE --> APPLY_COMMIT : APPLY_COMMIT
APPLY_COMMIT --> COMMITTED : commit_success

|Auditor|
REFUSED --> NULL_SPACE : emit_sentient_lock
NULL_SPACE --> NULL_SPACE_ISOLATED : archival_and_privileged_recovery

|Executor|
COMMITTED --> [*]

|Auditor|
NULL_SPACE_ISOLATED --> [*] : manual_recovery

note right of COMMITTED : State applied. WakeChain Event Emitted.
note left of NULL_SPACE_ISOLATED : Privileged zone. No edges return to runtime.

@enduml